ntdll: a long log line must not kill the process

`info->output` is `char[1020]`, and a line that does not fit in what is left
of it killed the process outright: `RtlRaiseStatus( STATUS_BUFFER_OVERFLOW )`
on the PE side, `abort()` on the unix side. The unix diagnostic was worse
than useless -- it printed the buffer's *previous* contents, naming an
innocent line rather than the one that overflowed.

Nothing in Wine emits lines that long. The components running on top of it
do: FEX and vkd3d both format into 4096-byte buffers and pass the result
straight to the debug channel, and DXVK is the only one of the three that
checks the length first. Wine's own unix side can also reach it unaided --
`wine_dbg_vprintf` buffers into `char buffer[1024]`, so 1023 characters with
no newline is enough.

What makes this worth fixing rather than working around is *when* it fires.
The probability rises with the amount of logging enabled, so it goes off
precisely when someone has turned channels up to diagnose something else, and
it presents as the program dying rather than as a logging fault. That is a
tracing bug wearing someone else's clothes.

Flush what is buffered, write an oversized line straight out, carry on.
Truncating instead was considered and rejected: a silently shortened log line
is a measurement that lies, which is worse than a long one.

Rebased from the Proton 11 tree this was written against; 11.14's context
around both functions differs, and the unix half there used fprintf where
this uses write.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/thread.c b/dlls/ntdll/thread.c
index fe083befbca..e15279e69d7 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/thread.c
@@ -72,11 +72,30 @@ static int append_output( struct debug_info *info, const char *str, size_t len )
 {
     if (len >= sizeof(info->output) - info->out_pos)
     {
-        __wine_dbg_write( info->output, info->out_pos );
-        info->out_pos = 0;
-        ERR_(thread)( "debug buffer overflow:\n" );
-        __wine_dbg_write( str, len );
-        RtlRaiseStatus( STATUS_BUFFER_OVERFLOW );
+        /* Vessel: flush and pass through rather than raise.
+         *
+         * info->output is char[1020], and a line longer than what is left in it
+         * killed the process outright -- RtlRaiseStatus here, abort() in the
+         * unix half. Nothing in Wine produces lines that long, but the
+         * components running on top of it do: FEX and vkd3d both format into
+         * 4096-byte buffers and hand the result straight to the debug channel,
+         * and DXVK is the only one that checks first.
+         *
+         * That makes it a *tracing* bug rather than a component bug: it gets
+         * more likely the more logging is switched on, so it fires exactly when
+         * someone is trying to diagnose something else. Truncation would be the
+         * other option and is worse -- a silently shortened log line is a
+         * measurement that lies. */
+        if (info->out_pos)
+        {
+            __wine_dbg_write( info->output, info->out_pos );
+            info->out_pos = 0;
+        }
+        if (len >= sizeof(info->output))
+        {
+            __wine_dbg_write( str, len );
+            return len;
+        }
     }
     memcpy( info->output + info->out_pos, str, len );
     info->out_pos += len;
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/debug.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/debug.c
index cfa57c50881..df0e9f9da0c 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/debug.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/debug.c
@@ -76,9 +76,25 @@ static int append_output( struct debug_info *info, const char *str, size_t len )
 {
     if (len >= sizeof(info->output) - info->out_pos)
     {
-       fprintf( stderr, "wine_dbg_output: debugstr buffer overflow (contents: '%s')\n", info->output );
-       info->out_pos = 0;
-       abort();
+        /* Vessel: the unix half of the same change as dlls/ntdll/thread.c's
+         * append_output -- see the long comment there for who produces lines
+         * this long and why. This half was the worse of the two: it abort()ed
+         * the process, and the diagnostic it printed named the *previous*
+         * buffer contents rather than the line that overflowed it.
+         *
+         * wine_dbg_vprintf's own buffer is char buffer[1024]
+         * (include/wine/debug.h), so Wine's unix side can reach this without
+         * any external component involved: 1023 characters and no newline. */
+        if (info->out_pos)
+        {
+            write( 2, info->output, info->out_pos );
+            info->out_pos = 0;
+        }
+        if (len >= sizeof(info->output))
+        {
+            write( 2, str, len );
+            return len;
+        }
     }
     memcpy( info->output + info->out_pos, str, len );
     info->out_pos += len;
